  "historical_output_text": " A common weather pattern is the seasonal change from spring to summer. \n\nIn spring, the sun's rays hit the Earth at a lower angle, warming the surface and melting snow and ice. This warming causes moisture from the ground to rise into the atmosphere, forming clouds and leading to more precipitation. \n\nAs spring progresses into early summer, the angle of the sun's rays becomes more direct. This increased solar radiation heats up the land and ocean surfaces even more. The warm air near the surface rises, creating areas of low pressure. Meanwhile, cooler air from higher altitudes flows in to replace the rising warm air, creating areas of high pressure",
